  "note": "(anim-guard) The guard's hands on the holder's forearm at the throat (BRIEF \"Holding a guard\": hands up at Wren's arm): both hands at chin height just in front of the throat, elbows down and out, the hands hooked over the forearm; a slight struggle: one hand pulls down while the chin turns into the elbow's crook, a heave with both hands and the head back against the arm, a re-grip, then the other side. A full-body standing cycle (the pair standing still, feet planted parallel 4 cm ahead of the root, the weight behind the heels) whose arm and wrist channels are meant to layer over guard_held_stumble while walking (its trunk is the stumble's mean). About 2.4 s a cycle (time driven). Keys 0-0.375 are mirrored onto 0.5-0.875. Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up); pelvis offsets in cm from rest (Wren 1.68 m). Arms: flex (+ forward, chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward (the forearm turned in), wrist { yaw (twist about the forearm), pitch, roll } local to the forearm (anim-rig, RIG.md). Legs (preview and floor checks; the game feet come from the foot planner until a leg channel exists): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up). Keyed by hand from how a real person moves (no game reference); the feet were placed on the floor and the hands on the holder's forearm with a two-bone IK while authoring, then written here as plain angles: edit these numbers directly.",
